    "title": "Unhappy Hour at Edgar Allan Poe Museum in Richmond, Virginia",
    "text": "4 hours ago Edgar Allan Poe Museum Photo by Poe Museum Screenshot UnHappy Hour is the Poe Museum's monthly themed evening featuring live music, food trucks, and local brews in the museum's Enchanted Garden . It is advertised as \"a miserable time from six to nine.\"\nThe beloved UnHappy Hours take place on the fourth Thursday of each month from April through October.\nEach Unhappy Hour is a tongue-in-cheek on the traditional happy hour, swapping standard corporate vibes for Edgar Allan Poe-themed commiseration.\nThe Poe Museum Photo by Facebook Screenshot \"Westward Poe Unhappy Hour\" Every Unhappy Hour has a specific theme. The upcoming \"Westward Poe UnHappy Hour\" is a western-themed event. Key details include:\nTime & Date: Thursday, July 23rd, from 6:00 PM to 9:00 PM. Music: Performances by Mary Moore and the HOTPANTS BAND. Food & Drinks: Beers from Kindred Spirit Brewing and southern fare from the 1115 Mobile Kitchen. Location: 1914 East Main Street, Richmond, VA 23223. Tickets: Available through the Richmond CultureWorks Calendar or directly on the Poe Museum Events Page .\n2",
    "summary": "The beloved UnHappy Hours take place on the fourth Thursday of each month from April through October. The upcoming \"Westward Poe UnHappy Hour\" is a western-themed event. Food & Drinks: Beers from Kindred Spirit Brewing and southern fare from the 1115 Mobile Kitchen. Location: 1914 East Main Street, Richmond, VA 23223. Tickets: Available through the Richmond CultureWorks Calendar or directly on the Poe Museum Events Page .",
